1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,140
One warning in the Bible
ends with "healed."

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:07,500
In Mark, when Jesus gives it,
it ends "forgiven."

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:10,120
Can one man give both?

4
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,760
Through Isaiah, God warns:
people will hear, but not understand,

5
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,980
or else they would turn back, and

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:19,180
"be healed."

7
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,320
Jesus repeats it.
What they would miss:

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,580
"their sins should be forgiven them."

9
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:29,540
In Matthew, Jesus says
they closed their own eyes.

10
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:32,520
A man who cannot walk is brought.

11
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:34,900
Jesus first says:

12
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:37,020
"Son, thy sins be forgiven thee."

13
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,520
Some sit thinking:
only God can forgive sins.

14
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,440
So Jesus heals him,

15
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:45,640
"that ye may know that the Son of man

16
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:50,460
hath power on earth to forgive sins."

17
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,820
He means Himself.
The man stands up and walks out.

18
00:00:54,860 --> 00:01:00,140
Forgiven, and healed.
Jesus has power to give both.

19
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:03,760
Turn back to God, and trust Jesus.

20
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:07,320
He forgives your sins,
and heals your heart.
